{"text": "exsooMiartemsar\n\nREAZ Q. KHAN\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nTo seek a water & wastewater treatment/engineering position with he City of Portland, OR.\n\nEXPERIENCE:\n\n09/05 \u2014 present Volunteer Trainee, CLARK COUNTY PUBLIC WORKS, Vancouver, WA.\n\nWastewater treatment plant operations training at Salmon Creek Wastewater Treatment Plant. Training\nareas include Preliminary Treatment, Primary Treatment, Aeration Basin, RAS/WAS Pumping Station,\nSecondary Clarifier,. Sludge Treatment, Digester, Solids Processing, Instrumentation & Process Control,\nPLC/SCADA System and Laboratory procedures. Reviewing plant engineering design reports, construction\ndrawings, as-built drawings and ongoing expansion engineering design and construction plans.\n\n01/98 - 06/04 Engineering & Technology Manager, GENESIS COMPUTER SYSTEMS, INC., Anaheim, CA.\n\nLed applications engineering and manufacturing teams for industtial-PC interface solutions fot a wide range\nof applications including petroleum drilling machines, chemical process equipment, telecom, access conttol,\nsecutity /video-surveillance and laboratory instruments. Performed systems integration, compatibility and\nhardwate-conflict resolutions, system testing, and application software installation and testing. Compiled\nequipment documentation and technical service manuals. Performed PC network administration for various\noffice environments including CAD, Engineering, Accounting and Office Automation. Provided training\nand technical support to clients and staff. Prepared quotations and proposals, negotiated contract terms,\nprepared manufacturing and assembly schedules, managed costs, billings and collections. Performed\ncustomer management and relationship development, including dispute resolution with minimal need for\n\nescalation. Introduced new products, services and upgrades.\n\n11/93 \u201412/97 Project Manager, AQUAMATCH, INC., Laguna Hills, CA.\n\nManaged all project phases of industrial, commercial and community water & wastewater treatment plant\nmanufacturing from bidding to commissioning and closeout. Prepared estimates, proposals and bid\npackages. Reviewed and interpreted contract tetms & conditions. Prepared project schedules and\nproactively addressed potential problems. Evaluated client bulletins, field ditectives & schedule changes and\nperformed associated cost estimates, negotiated settlements, and issued change orders. Performed\nsubcontractor and vendor management functions, including vendor qualification, negotiations, preparation,\nissuance of subcontracts, monitoring subcontractor progress and compliance, and dispute resolution.\nManaged all aspects of procurement, fabrication, installation, testing and commissioning. Oversaw project\nexecution for compliance with conttact terms, specifications, regulatory codes and engineeting practices.\nMonitored project schedules, costs/expenses, billings. Communicated project status/progress and finances\n\n. to corporate officers and client and issued alerts related to any actual or anticipated problems. Supervised\n\nengineering teams for process design, load analysis, system simulation, unit analysis, PFDs, MHBs and\nP&IDs, sizing piping, valves, pumps, designing piessure vessels, reactors, tanks, treatment plant structute\nand supports. Supervised design teams for CAD, 2D/3D modeling of plants using AutoCAD, preparation\nof bills of materials, fabrication and as-built drawings. Supervised systems engineering for instrumentation\nand control systems, instrumentation clusters, PLC based control panels, switchgear and motor control\ncabinets. Projects included 1.2 Million-GPD/1800psi-seawater desalination plant, 100 kGPD manufacturing\nwastewater treatment plant, 40 kGPD ultra putity industrial deionization unit, 80K GPD pharmaceutical\n\nPage 1 of. 2",
